WEBVTT

00:00.350 --> 00:05.627
Government teams work across policy, implementation guidance, standards,
governance minutes and decision records.

00:05.627 --> 00:14.151
Before advice is submitted or assurance is given, reviewers need the
authoritative source, the current wording and a clear route back

00:14.151 --> 00:15.369
to the evidence.

00:15.369 --> 00:22.270
When that trail is fragmented, skilled people spend time reconstructing
documentary context instead of judging the issue.

00:23.270 --> 00:30.897
A policy question can depend on the current policy, earlier wording,
implementation guidance, a standard, governance minutes and a

00:30.897 --> 00:31.699
recorded decision.

00:31.699 --> 00:33.706
A reference can be replaced.

00:33.706 --> 00:36.115
A date can change what applied.

00:36.115 --> 00:39.728
Local guidance may narrow how a policy is implemented.

00:39.728 --> 00:42.136
The challenge is not simply search.

00:42.136 --> 00:46.150
It is establishing authority, chronology and the relationships between
sources.

00:47.150 --> 00:52.501
Cortessa's target government-site deployment gives each authorised official a
dedicated, self-sufficient box.

00:52.501 --> 00:58.744
Permitted policy records, ingestion, index, on-device model and source viewer
remain on that box.

00:58.744 --> 01:02.757
Audit and Ask run locally against the approved corpus.

01:02.757 --> 01:06.325
Author remains in development and requires further testing.

01:06.325 --> 01:11.230
The official controls the working context, interpretation and every approved
revision.

01:12.230 --> 01:21.778
Official boxes are designed to connect through policy, delivery and assurance
departmental nodes to an on-site hub, entirely inside the

01:21.778 --> 01:22.732
air-gapped site.

01:22.732 --> 01:26.074
Department-default scope and selected sharing remain explicit.

01:26.074 --> 01:31.802
This is the target architecture, not a deployed-network, accreditation or
classification claim.

01:31.802 --> 01:38.486
The offline contract and application foundations exist; authenticated
transport, key operations, scheduling, backup, recovery,

01:38.486 --> 01:41.350
assurance and rollout remain deployment work.

01:42.350 --> 01:45.529
Audit is the centre of the Cortessa workflow.

01:45.529 --> 01:54.271
Across the bounded policy estate, it can surface a policy that cites a missing
standard, guidance that appears to rely on superseded

01:54.271 --> 01:59.437
wording, inconsistent terminology, uncertain effectivity or an unexplained gap
in the decision record.

01:59.437 --> 02:02.219
Each candidate enters an authorised review queue.

02:02.219 --> 02:06.590
It is not automatically a finding of legal or administrative non-compliance.

02:07.590 --> 02:11.757
Each audit result leads back to the passage that created it.

02:11.757 --> 02:17.818
The authorised reviewer can open the source, inspect surrounding wording and
confirm document state and chronology.

02:17.818 --> 02:22.364
If evidence is absent, Cortessa can refuse rather than fill the gap.

02:22.364 --> 02:29.183
The accountable official determines relevance, accepts or rejects the
candidate, and records the outcome through the existing process.

02:29.183 --> 02:33.350
Verified shows provenance; it does not establish policy correctness or
authority.

02:34.350 --> 02:41.926
Democratic accountability, statutory duties, policy intent and operational
context cannot be delegated to a language model.

02:41.926 --> 02:45.713
Cortessa can expose the evidence route and uncertainty.

02:45.713 --> 02:52.342
Accountable officials determine what applies, what it means and what
recommendation should be made.

02:52.342 --> 02:57.550
Cortessa does not take ministerial, policy, procurement, statutory or
regulatory decisions.

02:58.550 --> 03:05.449
An official-approved revision can carry signed identity, content hash, parent
lineage and approved audit context through its

03:05.449 --> 03:08.695
departmental node and, where authorised, the on-site hub.

03:08.695 --> 03:14.376
Conflicts remain explicit; the hub cannot make a public decision or choose
policy authority.

03:14.376 --> 03:18.434
Receipt does not certify, supersede or automatically index a record.

03:18.434 --> 03:25.738
The receiving official governs import and use, while the local Ledger supports
inspection without replacing statutory, security or

03:25.738 --> 03:26.550
records processes.

03:27.550 --> 03:31.132
Compare matched tasks against the current review workflow.

03:31.132 --> 03:37.848
Measure time to the authoritative source, traceability, stale-revision
visibility, accepted and rejected findings, correct refusals,

03:37.848 --> 03:39.638
reviewer effort and reproducibility.

03:39.638 --> 03:42.325
Record corpus preparation and setup burden.

03:42.325 --> 03:45.459
Include ambiguous policy language and absent records.

03:45.459 --> 03:53.070
The result should show where Cortessa helps, where it fails and what must
change before any expansion.

03:54.070 --> 03:58.740
Bring one appropriately controlled policy estate and the authorised officials.

03:58.740 --> 04:03.411
Test the evidence route and governed departmental exchange before expansion.

04:03.411 --> 04:08.081
Cortessa claims no government deployment, accreditation or completed site
rollout.

04:08.081 --> 04:11.350
Start a conversation about a scoped evaluation.
